<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <!-- Assembly name is the invoked command, so help usage and the MCP server name read "slnmap". -->
    <AssemblyName>slnmap</AssemblyName>
    <Description>Slnmap (sln-map) — a semantic map of your .sln for AI coding agents. Analyze a .NET solution into a queryable code graph, serve it over MCP, and inspect index status.</Description>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>slnmap</ToolCommandName>
    <PackageId>Slnmap</PackageId>
    <Version>0.14.0</Version>
    <RollForward>Major</RollForward>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 the Slnmap authors. All rights reserved.</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://slnmap.dev</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageTags>dotnet;roslyn;mcp;ai;code-analysis;claude-code;knowledge-graph</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Added: four new MCP tools (15 -> 19). find_unused_symbols (public/internal
symbols nothing references, caveat-first; overrides, interface implementations, entry points, tests
and generated files excluded and counted), get_attribute_usages (where an attribute is applied),
get_di_registrations (service -> implementation [lifetime] from your DI registrations; shapes that
can't be read statically are listed, never dropped), and find_callers_of_external (where the
solution calls into a package or the framework, by namespace prefix or assembly name).

Added: slnmap analyze --route-prefix states a prefix your app adds to controller routes at startup;
applied to controller endpoints only and marked [prefix: user-supplied]. Token-transformer-tolerant
route matching (ignores -/_ in [controller]/[action] segments when a RouteTokenTransformerConvention
is registered), tried last and always marked.

Added: projects analyzed without their dependencies (restore never ran or failed) are now
disclosed: a warning, a count in analyze and status, a one-line warning on every MCP answer, and a
Projects restored check in slnmap doctor. A change in restore state forces a full re-analysis.

Changed: route-convention disclosure now covers controller/action model conventions and
convention attributes, and is noted by the endpoint tools. Graph schema v2: the next analyze
rebuilds an existing graph automatically. The database is larger (+27-41%) and cold analyze
+6.5-9%.

Fixed: disclosure counters reset to zero on every incremental analyze and watch save.

Source: https://github.com/EMahmoudNabil/slnmap</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\viz-template.html" LogicalName="viz-template.html" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\vis-network.min.js" LogicalName="vis-network.min.js" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Analysis\Slnmap.Analysis.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Core\Slnmap.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Mcp\Slnmap.Mcp.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Storage\Slnmap.Storage.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Slnmap.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
